# AyurStock Pro: Bento Grid & Minimalist UI Overhaul

This plan outlines a complete top-to-bottom UI upgrade to transform AyurStock Pro into a highly professional, modern, and minimalist application using a Bento Grid design aesthetic.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Design Direction Approval**: Please review the proposed aesthetic changes below. 
> 
> **Key Decisions to make**:
> 1. **Color Palette**: I suggest moving to a highly premium "Zinc/Slate" base with a crisp, vibrant primary accent (like a deep Indigo or a refined Emerald Green) to replace the current standard blue/green mix. Does this sound good?
> 2. **Bento Grid**: The Dashboard and POS (Billing) screens will be heavily restructured into a modern "Bento Box" layout (tiles of varying dimensions). 
> 
> Let me know if you have specific preferences for colors or if you approve of my suggestions!

## Proposed Changes

### Global Theme & Design System

#### [MODIFY] [tailwind.config.js](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/tailwind.config.js)
- Overhaul the color palette to introduce sleek, minimalist variables (surface, muted, deep space).
- Add new `boxShadow` definitions for soft, premium elevations.
- Add specific `borderRadius` tokens (e.g., `3xl` for Bento cards).

#### [MODIFY] [app/globals.css](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/app/globals.css)
- Update the base background to a clean, professional off-white (`#FAFAFA`) or a subtle mesh gradient.
- Refine typography rules for tighter, modern tracking and line heights.
- Update structural CSS classes (like `.pos-container`) to match the new grid systems.

---

### Core Layout Components

#### [MODIFY] [components/Sidebar.tsx](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/components/Sidebar.tsx)
- Redesign from a standard blocky sidebar to a minimalist, modern navigation panel (floating or cleanly integrated).
- Use subtle active states (e.g., a small vertical pill indicator or soft background) instead of heavy highlights.
- Simplify typography and icon weights.

#### [MODIFY] [components/DashboardHeader.tsx](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/components/DashboardHeader.tsx)
- Streamline the header to be a clean, semi-transparent top bar.
- Add a unified, minimalist search input design.

---

### Key Page Redesigns (Bento Grid Application)

#### [MODIFY] [app/dashboard/page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/app/dashboard/page.tsx) (Main Dashboard)
- **Bento Overhaul**: Rebuild the statistics and charts into a dynamic, asymmetric grid layout.
- Use varying card sizes (e.g., large span for main sales chart, smaller squares for total medicines and alerts).
- Apply heavy `border-radius` and soft shadows.

#### [MODIFY] [app/dashboard/billing/page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/app/dashboard/billing/page.tsx) (POS Screen)
- Redesign the split layout to maximize efficiency while remaining visually clean.
- Bento-style layout for the cart, item grid, and action buttons.
- Modernize the receipt preview.

#### [MODIFY] [app/dashboard/medicines/page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/app/dashboard/medicines/page.tsx) & [app/dashboard/inventory/page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/app/dashboard/inventory/page.tsx)
- Overhaul data tables to be edge-to-edge inside crisp, borderless cards.
- Update action buttons (Add Medicine, Import) to match the new minimalist button components.
- Modernize all status badges (e.g., low stock, expired) to smooth pill shapes.

---

### UI Component Polish

#### [MODIFY] `components/ui/*` (Button, Input, Card, Dialog, etc.)
- Refine the Shadcn UI base components to fit the new specific theme.
- E.g., slightly rounder inputs, removing harsh borders in favor of soft fills (`bg-slate-100`), standardizing primary button gradients or flat solid colors.

#### [MODIFY] [components/ImportMedicinesModal.tsx](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/components/ImportMedicinesModal.tsx) & other Modals
- Update all dialogs to use the new minimalist overlay and container styles.

## Verification Plan

### Automated/Dev Testing
1. Use `npm run dev` and the internal browser agent to navigate through the application.
2. Visually inspect the newly added Tailwind classes and Bento Grid layouts across breakpoints (Desktop vs Mobile widths).

### Manual Verification
1. Click through all core flows (Login -> Dashboard -> Medicines -> Billing) to ensure all interactive elements (buttons, dropdowns, modals) remain fully functional post-styling.
2. Verify that the POS scaling and layout responsiveness did not break functional usability during the redesign.
